You asked for January run-rate - it's in section 7. These are platform
metering numbers, not finance actuals; Percy's figures after the January
close will replace them. Budget totals are kept out of the document on
purpose; that conversation belongs to Percy, not to a PDF.

What changed since v2:

  1. Tenancy model (s.1): quotas are now enforced at the gateway rather than
     advisory. A tenant that exceeds its quota gets 429s, not a polite email.
  2. Identity broker (s.2): per-tenant mapping of campus IdP groups to
     Kettleyard roles, so a campus can scope access without asking us.
  3. Model gateway (s.3): one shared connection pool per upstream provider
     with per-tenant shares, replacing the per-tenant pools from v2 (which
     were mostly idle and occasionally all busy at once, the worst of both).
  4. Secrets vault (s.4): per-tenant paths; API keys are now issued per
     tenant, not per application.
  5. Logging/redaction (s.5): the redaction filter now runs before the log
     sink, not after it. Prompt and response bodies are off by default.
  6. Onboarding (s.6): checklist rewritten around Tinderbox as tenant #1.
  7. New section 7: January run-rate, by component.
  8. Open questions (s.8): trimmed from 14 to 6. The other 8 either got
     answered or got demoted to "someone else's problem", which is also an
     answer.

Comments inline on the PDF or as a numbered list by email are both fine. If
you number them I will reply per number, which you know I enjoy.

